--- field object.account.sid
type: bin.sid

The security identifier (SID) of the account an event concerns.

The field names a stored principal whose credentials or account were
checked or changed. It records the SID rather than the mutable account
name. An account can exist without a live token; `object.token.sid`
instead names the user represented by a particular token.

--- field object.group.sid
type: bin.sid

The security identifier (SID) of the group an event concerns.

The field names a created or deleted group, or the group involved in a
membership change. It can identify a group in the source's own domain or
a well-known group such as `BUILTIN\Administrators`.

--- event lpsd.credential.verified
tier: standard
gating: none — every credential lpsd checks for a logon is recorded
cardinality: once per logon lpsd decides; probing which SSH keys an account would accept writes none

The local source checked a credential for a logon relayed by authd.

The event distinguishes an unknown account from an incorrect credential
for authorized audit readers. The authentication reply does not disclose
that distinction. Account names supplied by clients are never recorded;
an existing account is identified by its security identifier (SID).

A key-eligibility probe does not produce this event. Credential-free
logons are recorded with `operation.name` set to `none`. A successful
source check alone does not prove that a token reached the client; inspect
`authd.logon.attempted` for the authority's result.

This standard event records credential checks, which can occur more often
than successful sign-ins on a network-facing machine.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  lpsd itself, the principal that checked the credential: the user SID of
  lpsd's own token, which is its service account.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account the credential was checked for. Absent when lpsd holds no
  account by the name it was asked about.
field: operation.name                       required
  values: password | ssh-key | none
  closed: false
  What was checked. `none` is an account whose policy is that it signs in
  with no credential, asserted without asking for one.
field: outcome.success                      required
  True when lpsd told authd who the principal is.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: no-such-account | wrong-credential | disabled | not-permitted
  closed: false
  `not-permitted` is an account whose credential policy does not allow
  the kind of credential offered, or a key the account does not hold.

--- event lpsd.credential.changed
tier: essential
gating: none — every change of an account's own credential is recorded, and every refusal once the account is known
cardinality: once per change conversation that reaches the account

An account attempted to change its own password or enrolled public keys.

The conversation goes through authd, which identifies the caller and
relays proof to the local source. Success is recorded after the store save;
refusals are recorded once the affected account is known. An administrator's
credential changes instead produce `lpsd.account.modified`.

This essential event records changes to authentication material. See PSPU
§2.21 and §2.23 for the corresponding conversations.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The principal that asked, as authd vouched for them from their token.
  The same security identifier (SID) as `object.account.sid`: callers can
  change only their own credentials through this interface.
field: object.account.sid                   required
field: operation.name                       required
  values: password | ssh-key-added | ssh-key-removed
  closed: false
field: outcome.success                      required
  True once the change is durable.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: no-such-account | disabled | no-credential | wrong-credential | superseded | rejected | conversation-limit | not-saved
  closed: false
  `no-credential` is an account with no password to prove itself with;
  `superseded` a password that changed between the rounds of the
  conversation; `rejected` a new password or key the store refused;
  `conversation-limit` too many unusable new passwords; `not-saved` a
  change whose save failed. A failure after replacement can leave changed
  on-disk state; this reason does not prove that the change was unapplied.

--- event lpsd.account.created
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request

An administrator requested creation of a local account.

The request is recorded after authorization and dispatch, whether creation
succeeds or fails. The first-account provisioning service uses the same
administrative interface. Rejected connections and malformed requests that
do not reach dispatch are not represented by this event.

This essential event records creation of a persistent identity and its
initial authentication configuration.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator: the user security identifier (SID) of the requesting
  token.
field: object.account.sid                   when outcome.success == true
  The new account.
field: outcome.success                      required
  True once the account is durable.
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | exists | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  The failure `lps` was told: `not-found` names a group that does not
  exist, `exists` an account name already in use, `invalid` a value the
  store refuses, `not-saved` a change that could not be made durable.

--- event lpsd.account.deleted
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request

An administrator requested deletion of a local account.

Authorized requests that reach dispatch are recorded, including refusals.
The account's security identifier (SID) is retained in the record when the
account existed, even after deletion.

This essential event records removal of an identity that cannot be restored
by recreating its name. Deletion does not rewrite resource descriptors,
remove the home directory, or revoke already-issued tokens.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  `invalid` is a deletion the store refuses, such as of the last
  administrator.

--- event lpsd.account.modified
tier: essential
gating: administrative dispatch and self-service display-name requests; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

An administrator or account holder requested an account change.

Administrative changes use the admin socket. An account holder can change
their own display name through the self-service socket. `operation.name`
identifies the requested change. Authorization failures before
administrative dispatch are not recorded here.

A request that makes no change, such as turning on an already-active
account, produces no event. Dispatched failures are recorded. This essential
event records changes to identity attributes and authentication policy.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The principal that asked: an administrator, or the account itself for
  `set-display-name`.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account changed. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  For `set-primary-group`, the group made the account's primary group.
field: operation.name                       required
  values: set-enabled | set-password | set-profile | set-display-name | set-primary-group | set-claim | remove-claim | rename | set-logon-types | key-add | key-remove | set-credential-policy
  closed: false
  The change, as `lps` names its command. `set-display-name` is the
  principal's own, through the self socket.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | exists | invalid | internal | denied | not-saved
  closed: false
  `denied` is a disabled account changing its own display name.

--- event lpsd.group.created
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request

An administrator requested creation of a local group.

Authorized requests that reach dispatch are recorded, including refusals.
The group's security identifier (SID) appears only when creation succeeds.
This essential event records a new identity that access rules can name.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.group.sid                     when outcome.success == true
  The new group.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: exists | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.deleted
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request

An administrator requested deletion of a local group.

Authorized requests that reach dispatch are recorded, including refusals.
The group's security identifier (SID) is retained when the group existed.
The store refuses deletion while an account still belongs to the group or
uses it as its primary group.

This essential event records removal of a group identity. Deletion does not
rewrite resource descriptors or remove the SID from already-issued tokens.
Recreating the same name allocates a different SID.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.member.added
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

An administrator requested an account's membership in a group.

Authorized requests that reach dispatch are recorded, including refusals.
An already-existing membership produces no event. A group can be a local
identity or a well-known group such as `BUILTIN\Administrators`.

This essential event records a membership that affects later token creation.
It does not add the group to tokens already issued.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false

--- event lpsd.group.member.removed
tier: essential
gating: authorized requests reaching dispatch; unchanged successful requests produce no event
cardinality: once per request that changes something or fails

An administrator requested removal of an account's group membership.

Authorized requests that reach dispatch are recorded, including refusals.
A membership that did not exist produces no event. This essential event
records an access-policy change; removing the membership does not revoke
already-issued tokens that contain the group.

field: subject.token.sid                    required
  The administrator.
field: object.account.sid                   optional
  The account. Absent when no account had the name asked for.
field: object.group.sid                     optional
  The group. Absent when no group had the name asked for.
field: outcome.success                      required
field: outcome.reason                       when outcome.success == false
  values: not-found | invalid | internal | not-saved
  closed: false
  `invalid` includes removing the last administrator from
  `BUILTIN\Administrators`.
